p Last updated October 28, 2026.

p
  | This policy covers the apps made by Cezary Wojcik, and this website. It applies to every app that links here.

h2 Your data

p
  | The apps do not ask you to create an account. They do not sell your data, show ads, or include analytics or tracking.

p
  | What an app keeps for you, such as saved items, history, or settings, stays on your device. Widgets and other on-device features read that same data. Deleting the app removes it. I do not run a server that collects it.

h2 Location and other requests

p
  | An app uses your location only while you are using a feature that needs it, such as a map or a lookup at your current spot. The apps do not track your location in the background.

p
  | When a feature has to ask another service for an answer, such as a map from Apple or a public dataset for a place you picked, that request goes to the service that provides the answer. I do not receive a copy of it.
  a(href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/")  Apple's privacy policy
  |  describes how Apple handles requests it receives.

h2 Notifications

p If an app reminds you of something, that reminder is scheduled on your device. It is not sent through a server I run.

h2 This website

p
  | cezarywojcik.com is a separate personal site. The contact form emails me what you submit (including your IP address) so I can reply, and blog posts may load comments from Disqus. The apps do not include any of that.

h2 Contact

p
  | Questions about this policy or an app go through the
  a(href="/contact")  contact form
  |.

h2 Changes

p If these practices change, I will update this page. The date at the top is the latest revision.
